//     bit, all ones): permitted iff both bits read back 1, otherwise illegal-instruction (stval 0
//     or the instruction). The cases where the other bits are set check that no enable leaks
//     between counters.
//   Also (only this bit, only this bit), so a design that needs all enable bits set fails.
//   2. Zihpm: for hpmcounter3-31 (and high halves on RV32), with mcounteren all ones, scounteren
//     all ones, all but this bit, and only this bit: the same rule.
